---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro';
import { DISCUSSIONS, REPO } from '../lib/links';
import '../styles/pages.css';

const RUN_SERVER = `${REPO}#running-the-server`;
---
<Page title="Worgl Cloud" description="Worgl Cloud will run your mints for you, on the same open-source server you can run yourself. It is not available yet.">
  <section class="band paper cloud-hero edge edge-cobalt" data-tone="paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="bigstamp-edge">
        <div class="bigstamp">
          <span class="overprint" aria-hidden="true">Not available yet</span>
          <div class="corner"><span class="label">Worgl Cloud</span><span class="label">Hosted mints</span></div>
          <h1>Worgl <em>Cloud.</em></h1>
          <span class="label na tag">Not available yet</span>
          <p class="intro">Worgl Cloud will run your mints for you. You create a mint for each kind of token, mint to your own systems with your own authority key, and your holders use the SDKs. It runs the same open-source server you can run yourself.</p>
          <div class="act">
            <p>There is no waitlist and no form. Questions and ideas go to GitHub Discussions, in public.</p>
            <div class="ctas"><a class="btn btn-solid-paper" href={DISCUSSIONS}>Tell us what you'd build</a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band cobalt promises edge edge-paper" id="promises" data-tone="cobalt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <SectionHead num="01" name="Promises" />
      <div class="grid">
        <h2 class="h2">What it will <em>promise.</em></h2>
        <p class="body sec-aside">Four commitments, made before the service exists, so you can hold it to them.</p>
        <ol class="promise-list">
          <li><h3>Worgl never mints</h3><p>Worgl never mints, holds or redeems value. Only your authority key can mint.</p></li>
          <li><h3>One note per transfer</h3><p>Every hosted mint takes one note per transfer, so no transfer reveals that two notes share an owner.</p></li>
          <li><h3>Supply, not lineage</h3><p>You see supply and usage, never per-note events. Lineage is kept only until the next snapshot, plus seven days of backups.</p></li>
          <li><h3>Three zones</h3><p>Every mint is replicated across three zones, and no acknowledged transfer is lost when a server fails.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band paper stages edge edge-cobalt" id="where-it-stands" data-tone="paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <SectionHead num="02" name="Where it stands" />
      <div class="grid">
        <h2 class="h2 sec-intro">Three steps, no <em>dates.</em></h2>
        <p class="body muted sec-aside">Each step starts when the one before it has done what it says, not on a calendar.</p>
        <ol class="stage-row">
          <li class="now">
            <span class="stage-box" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
            <span class="label">In progress</span>
            <h3>Private alpha</h3>
            <p>Replication is built. Failover drills come next, and no one's mint runs on it until those drills lose nothing.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="stage-box" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
            <span class="label">Next</span>
            <h3>Beta</h3>
            <p>Free, with capacity quotas. Pricing is published before anyone is billed.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="stage-box" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
            <span class="label">Then</span>
            <h3>General availability</h3>
            <p>An availability target, prices and a bug bounty, after an independent security review.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <div class="self-host">
          <p class="lede">Until then, the server Worgl Cloud will run is yours to run today, alone or as a three-member cluster.</p>
          <div class="ctas"><a class="btn btn-solid" href={RUN_SERVER}>Run the server</a><a class="btn" href={DISCUSSIONS}>Tell us what you'd build</a></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
